    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1913" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">allecto</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adl-</span></b> ), āvi, ātum, 1,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq.</i>
			[id.], <i>to allure</i>, <i>to
			entice</i> (prob. only in the foll. exs.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad agrum fruendum non modo non retardat, verum
					etiam invitat atque adlectat senectus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Sen. 16 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Lael. 26, 98</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">boves sibilo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 3, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
